  "why_this_paper_matters": "This review provides context for mitochondrial dysfunction in systemic sclerosis (SSc), linking it to inflammaging and fibrosis through the cGAS-STING pathway. While it identifies mitochondrial stress as a key factor in SSc, it does not provide direct experimental evidence of mitochondrial dysfunction in human tissues or specific pathways. The review highlights the potential for therapeutic strategies targeting mitochondrial dysfunction in SSc, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm these mechanisms in human patients.",
